in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @nl
in @property
in @io

# @code/rust — the Rust altitude grammar.
#
# The altitude at which mosaic's shift delegates to cargo. When
# mirror.spec declares `target binary { altitude @code/rust, emit
# cargo }`, mosaic walks the target, resolves `@code/rust` here,
# then resolves `cargo` against this altitude's namespace —
# landing on the sub-prism `@code/rust/cargo` below.
#
# Lifts from boot/std/code/rust.mirror with the substrate-pull
# tightenings: no parser surface (parsing is @mirror/compile's
# job, not the altitude's), no Rust-AST type fragments (the body-
# lens contract moved to @mirror/compile's bootstrap; the altitude
# only declares the five-op signature and the build-property
# surface mosaic consumes).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-spec-schema.md §2 (target.emit),
# §10.5 (emit disambiguation), §4 (settle_on predicates);
# docs/specs/mosaic.md §4 (the @code/rust delegation contract).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Related shards: glass.mirror (verdict), mirror/mosaic.mirror
# (the consumer), mirror/spec.mirror (the schema).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/code/rust.mirror`
# declares `@code/rust` (and the path-nested sub-prism
# `@code/rust/cargo`). The macro-reception sub-prism
# `@code/rust/macro` lives alongside at `shards/code/rust/macro.mirror`
# (T23 — the language-side compile-time AST consumption surface;
# spec docs/specs/code-macro-surface.md).

prism @code/rust {
  focus rust
  project rust
  split rust
  shift rust
  settle rust
}

# === cargo — the emit-target sub-prism ===
#
# Per mirror-spec-schema.md §10.5: `emit` takes `ref(@io)` OR
# `ref(@code/*)` grammar; disambiguation is by type. The bare
# `emit cargo` in mirror.spec is resolved by searching the
# lexically enclosing target's altitude namespace first —
# @code/rust. `cargo` lives here as a sub-prism (the substrate-
# pull: the emit-target identity belongs to the altitude that
# emits, not to the @io module that invokes).
#
# Two distinct things share the name `cargo`:
#   - @code/rust/cargo  — THIS sub-prism. The emit-target
#                          substrate identity. What mirror.spec
#                          binds. Pure declaration; no I/O.
#   - @io.cargo         — D3, shards/io/cargo.mirror. The actual
#                          cargo invocation contract (build,
#                          test, lockfile, env, exit codes).
#                          Mosaic's `shift @code/rust` delegates
#                          through THIS sub-prism, which in turn
#                          calls @io.cargo.
prism @code/rust/cargo {
  focus cargo
  project cargo
  split cargo
  shift cargo
  settle cargo
}

# === build-property surface (settle_on consumers) ===
#
# mirror.spec's `settle_on { binary.compiles, binary.tests_pass }`
# block resolves these names against the binary target's altitude
# grammar (per spec §4 "Predicate sources"). Declared here as
# typed lambdas returning @glass.verdict so the spec parser can
# typecheck the settle_on block at spec-evaluation time.
#
# The obligation body (\) is discharged by @code/rust/cargo when
# it actually invokes cargo — `compiles` reads cargo's build exit
# code, `tests_pass` reads `cargo test`'s exit code. The contract
# is the verdict shape; the invocation is D3.

compiles(target) -> verdict { \ }
tests_pass(target) -> verdict { \ }

out @code/rust
out @code/rust/cargo
out compiles
out tests_pass
